Magni wrote:

> Out of sheer curiosity, what's the earliest possible corpse that'll
> give me poison resistance? And how much do amulets of proof against
> poison cost, usually?

Amulets are 1% of random objects in the main dungeon and in containers,
and amulet-vs-poison will be 16.5% of those.  If an unidentified
randomly-generated amulet is known not to be cursed, then the
probabilities are as follows -

Amulet of Change ... 2.03%
ESP ... 27.34% (my favourite early amulet)
Life Saving ... 11.72%
Magical Breathing ... 10.16%
Reflection ... 11.72%
Restful Sleep ... 2.11%
Strangulation ... 2.11%
Unchanging ... 7.03%
Versus Poison ... 25.78%

Also, 2.1% of randomly-generated cursed amulets will be versus-poison,
but don't go chancing it because 92.35% of such amulets are bad for
you.  With a not-cursed amulet, try it on and if it is not ESP, Change,
Restful Sleep or Strangulation (all easily identified) then it is
better than a 1 in 3 chance (38.82%) of being amulet-vs-poison.

You didn't ask about rings of poison resistance, which are 1/28th of
all randomly-generated rings and which have a base price of 150
zorkmids (along with 9 other types of ring).  There are three times as
many rings as amulets in the dungeon, but of all randomly-generated
objects the amulet is about 54% more likely than the ring.  One in 933
r.g.o's will be a ring of poison resistance; one in 606 will be an
amulet-vs-poison.

Both the ring and the amulet will be more common (than the base
probabilities) amongst rings and amulets in bones piles high in the
dungeon, because low-level characters without intrinsic poison
resistance and with a low carrying capacity are likely to keep those
objects and stash or abandon others. Conversely, a bones pile below
Minetown or Sokoban is very unlikely to have such a ring or amulet -
the player dying at that depth typically has the intrinsic and has
sold/polymorphed/stashed/abandoned the artificial aid.

The lowest level monster whose corpse *might* give you poison
resistance is a killer bee, but in practice I have encountered
unicorns, brown molds and homonculi earlier and higher in the dungeon
than killer bees in numerous games, and those corpses are also good for
the desired result (although they'll cause you damage as you eat).

